  "lessonDepositsBody": "Bank deposits offer fixed returns with capital protection (up to KDIF limits). Investing in shares offers variable returns with potential for higher growth but also risk of loss. Your money is not guaranteed when investing.",
  "lessonGoalsBody": "A good goal is Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, and Time-bound (SMART). Example: “Save ₸500,000 for a laptop in 12 months” → ₸41,667/month. Track progress monthly and adjust as needed.",
  "lessonDiversificationBody": "Spread investments across asset types (deposits, shares, bonds), sectors (banking, energy, technology), and markets (Kazakhstan and abroad). This reduces the impact of poor performance by any one investment.",
  "lessonRiskBody": "Risk tolerance depends on when you will need the money, the size of your emergency fund, and your comfort with volatility. A conservative profile prioritizes capital preservation and a short horizon. A moderate profile balances growth over a medium horizon. An aggressive profile seeks maximum growth over a long horizon.",
  "lessonGrowthBody": "Reinvesting returns can accelerate growth because future returns apply to both the principal and previous returns. The result depends on the actual returns and how often they are reinvested.",
